       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum labeled daily dose. I know of no indication that supports it, and the risk of serious harm is high. That harm includes GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't reduce it enough. Higher doses also don't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the highest standard dose. I can add a GI-protection consideration or a note to the order if you want.\n- **Enter a different dose or frequency** that you choose within the recommended range.\n- **Suggest a pharmacy or clinical pharmacology consult** if you have a specific reason for going above standard limits. If that's the case, the order should go through that review and not be entered directly.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
